 "_about": "parens (2026-10-30): parentheses group conditions in the filter text. Every query runs through the THREE engines - main.js parseAdvancedQuery + evaluateParsedQuery (harness.html, headless Edge), penumbra_search.php php_apply_search_filter and schedule_runner.php parse_format_condition + evaluate_format_condition (php_side.php, the runner through a mirror) - and each must return exactly expect (row IDs). paren = a reading the old engines got wrong (the control is red there); noFormat = nested columns, which the scheduler's format engine does not read. Two grouped queries carry no paren mark: the old engines read `C = yes)` as C = yes (the equality strips punctuation), so `(zq or A = no) and C = yes` and `(K = b or V = 1)` happened to come out right before; they still pin the three engines to one answer.",
 "columns": ["#", "ID", "A", "B", "C", "D", "SUBS"],
